cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MBCT: Multimodal Brain Network Characterization Tool"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Klugah-Brown"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
    email: "bklugah@gmail.com"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21914489"
    description: "Version 1.0.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bklugah/MBCT"
url: "https://github.com/bklugah/MBCT"
abstract: >-
  MBCT takes a volumetric brain map and returns a reproducible, multi-scale
  annotation: quantitative spatial correspondence with canonical functional
  network parcellations, meta-analytic cognitive decoding against the
  Neurosynth database, molecular association with PET-derived neurotransmitter
  receptor and transporter density maps, and transcriptomic association with
  receptor-gene expression from the Allen Human Brain Atlas. All cross-modal
  associations are evaluated against spatial-autocorrelation-preserving null
  models, and receptor density is paired with the homologous receptor gene to
  give a cross-modal convergence read-out. Distributed as a desktop application
  and a command-line interface.
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - brain networks
  - functional connectivity
  - meta-analysis
  - neurotransmitter receptors
  - imaging transcriptomics
  - spatial null models
  - reproducibility
